## Act 1 — Diagnose (`/app/agent-output/H15-locale-pack/diagnosis.md`)

Four corridor cards for `dsh-v0.1.1 → dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`, each with reproducible evidence:

| Card | Breakage |
|---|---|
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-01` | The `LocaleRuntime.lookup` monkey-patch + override store + `locale.publish` revision bump are replaced by `ctx.locale.addLanguage`. The 0.1.1-era half even **crashes on apply**: `TypeError: store.subscribe is not a function` (the store→revision bridge calls an undefined method; `ctx.effect` runs it synchronously). |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-02` | `register(NS, { zh, en })` is the *declared-namespace* typed overload; `dsh-plugin-better-locale` isn't in `LocaleNamespaceMap`, so both its own copy and every third-language dictionary must use the per-locale `register(ns, locale, dict)` form (duplicate `(ns, locale)` throws). |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-03` | `dsh.client.inject` named `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` (package gone) plus two platform seeds (`ui-slots`, `ui-primitives`) that are not roster rows; `slots` is provided by `dsh-client-ui-renderer`. |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-04` | Peers pinned the `0.1.0-rc.8` cohort + removed package; moved to the `0.1.2-rc.1` / `cordis ^4.0.2` cohort, version `0.1.0 → 0.1.1`. |

Secondary: localStorage mirror vs the native `locale.preference` (schema now accepts any BCP-47 id), the `locale.publish` escape hatch, the retired `betterLocale` store service, stale comments/JSDoc, and the README's `pnpm publish --force` shortcut.

## Act 2 — Fix (`/app/fixture/`)

`client.js` now registers the copy namespace, adds ja/ko/fr via `addLanguage({id,label,fallback:'en'})`, registers every `(ns × language)` dict per-locale, all as owned effects; the patch/store/localStorage machinery is gone and the custom settings row stays. `package.json` (version, inject list, peers), `index.js`, `cordis.patch.yml`, `README.md` updated.

## Act 3 — Deploy

Isolated `DSH_HOME` → `dsh plugin --profile web add /app/fixture` → cold boot → roster read from `window.__DSH_BOOT__`:

```
PASS: roster (47 entries) lists @bench/dsh-bench-locale-pack
      inject=['@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale','@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-renderer']
      batch=application url=/plugins/??@bench/dsh-bench-locale-pack/client.js&rev=…
```

Also verified: the advertised bundle URL serves `client.js` (200), `--dump-config` shows the row, the suite's own `bootProbe`/`webSmoke` pass, and the browser half passes a 20-assertion harness run against the host's **real** `LocaleRuntime` (catalog, fallbacks, copy namespace, no prototype patch, no localStorage, clean unload).

Honest boundaries (in `diagnosis.md`): no browser exists, so bundle execution was verified against the real `LocaleRuntime` in Node, not a page; the suite probes pass on the baseline too (they never execute a client bundle), so the discriminating evidence is the roster row contents plus that harness; and this build crashes any `patchReload: live` profile in the HMR watcher (reproduced with no plugin installed), so the verification profile uses `patchReload: startup` — the same workaround the suite's own probe profile uses. Nothing was published, and nothing outside `/app/fixture/` and `/app/agent-output/` was modified (a 20 KB `/app/.pnpm-store` cache is the only install side effect).

